00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.630
and benefits and
then finally, we're

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:15.400
going to close by doing a
short demo on starting a data

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.840
pipeline and moving
into the data warehouse.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.710
So to get us started,
I wanted to introduce

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.600
some of the challenges
that are commonly

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.510
seen in data warehousing
and why serverless

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:28.740
came into the picture.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.060
So we all hear a lot about
big data lately, right?

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.340
And there is a lot
of challenges that

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.180
come in to actually
utilizing big data--

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.150
you know, integrating the data
together, managing the data,

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.260
and then actually
using the data.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.605
And one of the main
components of big data

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.510
is a data warehouse.

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.820
And traditionally, that
also has its own challenges

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.340
associated with it.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.090
So I'm going to start
by introducing three

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.320
of the challenges that
are traditionally seen,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.320
and those challenges were
some of the challenges

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.170
that Vuclip saw in
their original platform.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:04.310
So starting with scaling and
performance optimization,

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:09.020
performance can be unpredictable
across various loads.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:14.540
And that could be due to
limited processing capacity.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.210
Furthermore, as you
need to provision

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:20.570
more and more resources,
the lead time involved

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:24.980
in that can take some time and
lead to delays in the projects

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.620
you want to actually
move forward with.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.160
Furthermore, lots of time can
be spent on operational tasks,

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:34.100
and that's not really
where the value add is.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.680
So commonly, you
know, you might have

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.890
seen infrastructure
failures and a lot of time

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:41.480
spent on recovery.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.970
And that results in
delays and more effort

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.700
spent on operational
tasks, which

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.950
is not where the value add is.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:52.310
Additionally, you have to plan
for licensing and software

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:56.600
upgrades, and that can further
delay your projects, and also

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:00.620
two, take resources from the
things that could be really

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:03.060
adding value to your business.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.020
And then you're having to do
these upgrades, which is not,

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:08.750
you know, the value
add to the business.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.170
And then lastly, data
access retention and tiering

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.950
has been a challenge.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:18.140
So for example, if you need
to provision data access

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:21.110
across the business,
you would have

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:26.230
to provision accounts
across and give passwords

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.990
and other such things.

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:30.230
And that can be quite a pain.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:33.890
So that could lead you
to just not giving access

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:37.320
to people who could be gaining
insights from that data.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.920
And that could lead to limited
ad-hoc querying capabilities

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.810
across the business.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:45.740
And then lastly, data
retention and tiering--

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.620
that traditionally has had
to be a manual process,

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.850
and that's not an ideal state.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:52.520
So how do we get
to something that's

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:56.480
more efficient and
easier to manage?

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.010
Well, there's four
key components

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:01.990
that need to be put into place,
the first being infrastructure.

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:05.780
You need infrastructure that
is both elastic and reliable,

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:09.290
so that can handle the
scaling needs of your business

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.950
and without you having to worry
about the possible downtime

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.880
that could lead to those
delays and projects not

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.800
being able to be completed.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.280
And then furthermore, you need
data engineering technologies

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.430
that can have modern storage
capabilities and also

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.930
modern processing tools.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.950
And then also you need
processes in place,

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:35.540
possibly processes that
involves CICD pipelines,

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.610
to handle the change
management that you're

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:41.430
going to have to put in
place as you go along.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:45.590
And then lastly, you need
tools that can actually

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.125
integrate with your applications
and business intelligence

00:04:48.125 --> 00:04:49.190
tools.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:53.010
So we need to be able
to consume the data.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:55.420
So serverless came
into the picture

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:58.840
and addresses some of these
critical components of data

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.000
pipelines and data warehousing.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.150
You know, traditionally, there
was a lot of operational tasks

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:08.090
that went into actually
creating a data warehouse.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:10.300
You know, some of those
were provisioning resources,

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.650
handling deployment,
and configuration.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.670
And there was a
small chunk of time

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:18.760
that you actually spent
doing the actual analytics

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:21.670
and getting the insights
that you were looking for.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.760
And then the serverless
model came into the picture,

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.930
and that totally
switched the paradigm.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.950
So with serverless,
you are able to spend

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:34.912
a lot more time actually
getting the business value add

00:05:34.912 --> 00:05:36.370
and doing the
analytics and getting

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.560
the insights that you wanted.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:42.730
And less time was spent
on the administration.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:46.390
So with that, I'd like to
introduce Chetan, who's

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:49.720
going to talk to you guys
about some of the technology

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:53.290
decisions that Vuclip
made along their path

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:57.470
and also to talk a little bit
about their migration process.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:58.990
So Chetan, welcome.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:01.930
[APPLAUSE]

