00:28:26.390 --> 00:28:31.100
and everywhere, we are talking
about how these components

00:28:31.100 --> 00:28:33.470
and utilities are changing
so that we can keep updated

00:28:33.470 --> 00:28:35.670
with the latest features.

00:28:35.670 --> 00:28:42.570
So what are the results and
benefits from all of this?

00:28:42.570 --> 00:28:46.130
So this is now the
latest footprint

00:28:46.130 --> 00:28:48.220
that we have in Google Cloud.

00:28:48.220 --> 00:28:51.350
There are around 40 plus
streaming pipelines, 50

00:28:51.350 --> 00:28:54.740
plus BigQuery data sets,
as many GCS buckets,

00:28:54.740 --> 00:28:57.860
talking about 75 plus
terabytes of data.

00:28:57.860 --> 00:29:00.500
There are 100 billion
rows of data in all.

00:29:00.500 --> 00:29:04.400
And we're talking about 300 to
400 million events every day.

00:29:04.400 --> 00:29:05.930
And there are 1,000
plus pipelines

00:29:05.930 --> 00:29:09.050
that are getting
spawned and destroyed

00:29:09.050 --> 00:29:10.440
after the work is done.

00:29:10.440 --> 00:29:13.220
So we don't really have
to worry about any kind

00:29:13.220 --> 00:29:15.258
of infrastructure management.

00:29:18.400 --> 00:29:21.250
The benefits are,
first of all, reduced

00:29:21.250 --> 00:29:22.570
redundant infrastructure.

00:29:22.570 --> 00:29:25.150
We always see that.

00:29:25.150 --> 00:29:27.190
Earlier, we had
in-house data platform.

00:29:27.190 --> 00:29:29.990
Now, you know, we don't really
have to manage anything.

00:29:29.990 --> 00:29:33.370
And once the use case is served,
it just tears down itself.

00:29:33.370 --> 00:29:39.640
High availability-- so earlier,
if certain traffic increased,

00:29:39.640 --> 00:29:41.800
then we would
basically see failures

00:29:41.800 --> 00:29:44.680
in some of the components
which would actually cause,

00:29:44.680 --> 00:29:46.360
you know, availability
to be hampered.

00:29:46.360 --> 00:29:48.540
But now that doesn't
happen anymore.

00:29:48.540 --> 00:29:50.840
Faster implementations--
earlier,

00:29:50.840 --> 00:29:55.220
our implementation time used
to span around three days.

00:29:55.220 --> 00:30:00.880
Now it has been
reduced to 30 minutes.

00:30:00.880 --> 00:30:04.780
Infrastructure management
overhead-- around two people

00:30:04.780 --> 00:30:07.870
use to actually
continuously do something

00:30:07.870 --> 00:30:09.910
to keep the in-house
infrastructure up.

00:30:09.910 --> 00:30:13.570
Now they are freed and they
can do something better.

00:30:13.570 --> 00:30:15.520
On-demand scale up
and scale down--

00:30:15.520 --> 00:30:18.520
so around 35
transactions per second

00:30:18.520 --> 00:30:20.590
to 500 transactions
per second is just

00:30:20.590 --> 00:30:22.060
supported without any change.

00:30:22.060 --> 00:30:24.310
The App Engine and
Dataflow instances

00:30:24.310 --> 00:30:28.330
just scale up by themselves
and then again scale down.

00:30:28.330 --> 00:30:30.710
On the ML and advanced
analytics front,

00:30:30.710 --> 00:30:33.450
ready-made and
battle-tested algorithms--

00:30:33.450 --> 00:30:36.280
as I said, we just need
a very little amount

00:30:36.280 --> 00:30:38.760
of coding to start them using.

00:30:38.760 --> 00:30:40.010
And faster value realization--

00:30:40.010 --> 00:30:43.550
I mean, this is one of the areas
that I really love about it.

00:30:43.550 --> 00:30:45.400
So we wanted to make changes.

00:30:45.400 --> 00:30:48.070
We want to respond to
business quickly rather than

00:30:48.070 --> 00:30:50.860
